  "_comment": "The untracked third-party payload a build or a shipped exe reads (tools/fetch_deps.py; ENGINE_REVIEW_2026-10-25 F1 / N1). Git holds these dependencies' headers and not their libraries, DLLs or prebuilt trees. 'include' / 'optionalInclude' are glob patterns under 'root' (relative to DX12/external); 'files' / 'optionalFiles' are what they matched when the manifest was written (python tools/fetch_deps.py --write-manifest --from <checkout>): size and sha256 of each. A file in 'files' must exist and match; one in 'optionalFiles' is checked when present. 'source.url' is where a fresh clone downloads the dep from - empty until decision D-3 (where the payload is hosted) is made; until then 'python tools/fetch_deps.py --from <a checkout that has them>' copies from one. RTXDI and SHARC are vendored from archives git tracks (vendor_rtxdi.py, vendor_sharc.py) and ONNX Runtime from a pinned download (vendor_onnxruntime.py): not listed here.",
